# OffboardAGV — deregister an AGV from the master. Wraps
# VDA5050Master::offboard_agv. Service half of Task #54.
#
# **What offboarding does master-side**:
#   - Removes the AGV from the master's onboard list.
#   - Calls AGV::stop() which (per agv.cpp): unsubscribes from MQTT
#     topics, clears state mutexes, drops outbound queues.
#   - Subsequent service calls referencing this AGV (assign_order,
#     get_device_status, get_order_status, etc.) return
#     AGV_NOT_ONBOARDED.
#
# **Idempotency**: offboarding a non-onboarded AGV returns
# NOT_ONBOARDED. FMS clients can call this safely without first
# checking onboarded state.

string manufacturer
string serial_number
---
# Status enum.
#
# SUCCESS         — AGV successfully offboarded; MQTT subscriptions
#                   torn down; AGV instance destroyed.
# NOT_ONBOARDED   — no AGV with this {manufacturer, serial_number}
#                   was found in the master's onboard list.
#                   Idempotent no-op; treat as success.
# INVALID_REQUEST — empty manufacturer or serial_number.
uint8 SUCCESS=0
uint8 NOT_ONBOARDED=1
uint8 INVALID_REQUEST=2
uint8 status

# Echo of request — async-fanout correlation.
string manufacturer
string serial_number
